From f9902799972641590e24e3c7284785835840cb0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:07:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 58/88] xhttp: data written before a close is sent

sing-box closes a connection as soon as its source is done. The session then
cancelled its requests at once and dropped what packet-up had not posted yet:
of 10 connections that sent data and closed, the destination got the data of
none in packet-up, of 2 to 9 in the stream modes (the Xray client: all 10).

A closed session now ends its upload first: packet-up posts what is pending
and waits for the answers, a streamed upload ends its request body and waits
for it to be written (stream-one) or answered (stream-up). When the server has
not answered the data since it was written, the session stays one more second
for the server to forward it, as an outbound of Xray does after the end of an
upload; 5 seconds bound the whole. A session whose last write was answered, the
usual end of an exchange, is taken down at once as before: 10000 short
sessions cost the same time and memory as they did.
